#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""netmap -- live network topology map for the terminal.

Plots your machine's real TCP connections onto a dot-matrix world map:
great-circle arcs to each remote endpoint, packets travelling along them at a
rate driven by actual throughput, a live day/night terminator, and a scrolling
event log.  Pure stdlib, no network calls of its own beyond reverse DNS.

    ./netmap.py                 # just run it
    ./netmap.py --palette ice   # pick a colour scheme
    ./netmap.py --home 51.5,-0.13
    ./netmap.py --demo          # synthetic traffic, for when you're offline

Press h in-app for the key bindings.

Geolocation is COUNTRY-LEVEL: endpoints are drawn at their country's centroid
with a small deterministic scatter so they don't stack.  A dot is not a
street address.

IP-to-country data derived from the DB-IP lite database (CC-BY-4.0,
https://db-ip.com).  Coastlines from Natural Earth (public domain).
"""

